Subject: [PATCH] userspace: keep generated kobject unwind layout stable

With CONFIG_USERSPACE and CONFIG_EXCEPTION_STACK_TRACE, the preliminary
link uses weak kobject lookup stubs while the final link substitutes gperf
implementations.  The generated wordlist iterator is non-leaf and needs its
own Arm unwind entry, but the empty stub is a leaf.  The final .ARM.exidx
therefore grows by eight bytes after gen_isr_tables.py and
gen_kobject_list.py have recorded absolute device addresses.

That shifts every following init/device object while leaving the generated
ISR arguments and kobject keys at their preliminary addresses.  Make the
stub non-leaf too, so the preliminary and final unwind tables have identical
shape.  The weak function is never called in the finished image because the
generated strong implementation replaces it.

diff --git a/kernel/userspace.c b/kernel/userspace.c
--- a/kernel/userspace.c
+++ b/kernel/userspace.c
@@ -566,7 +566,16 @@ __weak struct k_object *z_object_gperf_find(const void *obj)
 }
 Z_GENERIC_SECTION(.kobject_data.text.dummies)
 __weak void z_object_gperf_wordlist_foreach(_wordlist_cb_func_t func, void *context)
 {
+	/*
+	 * Match the generated iterator's non-leaf unwind shape. Otherwise its
+	 * extra final-link .ARM.exidx entry shifts device objects after the
+	 * generators have captured their preliminary absolute addresses.
+	 */
+	struct k_object *(*volatile find)(const void *) = z_object_gperf_find;
+
+	(void)func;
+	(void)find(context);
 }
 #else
 Z_GENERIC_SECTION(.kobject_data.text.dummies)
